//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// A `Tensor` spelled without its shape used to mean four unrelated things at once: a shape
// the type system had erased, a shape known only at run time, a scalar, and the checker's
// "I do not know" value. The two compilers even read it two different ways -- the flat path
// as rank 0, the AST path as rank 2 dynamic (Vx#399, Vx#409). Each meaning now has its own
// spelling, so the ambiguous one is gone rather than diagnosed case by case.
//
// RUN: not vxc %s 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: Tensor needs its shape
// CHECK-SAME: Tensor<f32, [2, 3]>
// CHECK-SAME: Tensor<f32, []>
// CHECK-SAME: DynTensor<f32>
fn erased(t : Tensor<f32>) -> i32 {
  return 0;
}

fn main() -> i32 {
  return 0;
}
